            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Empedokles' Life</strong><br>\nEmpedokles was a Greek philosopher, statesman, poet, and a scientist who lived in Sicily in the fifth century BCE. He was born in Acragas, now Agrigento, in Sicily, around 490 BCE. Empedokles was known for his wealth, strong personality, and influence. His fame extended beyond his hometown, and his ideas were known throughout Greece. Although his exact date of death is uncertain, he is believed to have died around 430 BCE.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Philosophical Contributions</strong><br>\nEmpedokles is best remembered for introducing the theory of the four classical elements. He proposed that all matter was made up of four roots: earth, air, fire, and water. These elements, he believed, were unchangeable and formed the basis of the world through their mixture and separation. His work laid early foundations for later scientists and philosophers to build upon.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Involvement</strong><br>\nEmpedokles also played a significant role in the local politics of Acragas. He was involved in overthrowing a ruling oligarchy and setting up a democratic government. His influence in politics was due in part to his noble birth and his reputation for wisdom and oratory skills. He was considered a champion of the people and democracy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
