          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence on Medicine</strong><br>\nHis ideas had a significant impact on the development of medicine. Empedokles was among the first to suggest that the human body was composed of the same elements as the rest of the cosmos, influencing the health and disease concepts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Religious and Mystical Beliefs</strong><br>\nEmpedokles was known for his belief in reincarnation and divine retribution. He claimed to have been a god in a previous life and that his soul was punished for a past sin by being forced to become mortal. These beliefs were interwoven with his philosophical and scientific theories.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Memory</strong><br>\nEmpedokles' impact on philosophy, science, and politics was profound. His four-element theory persisted into the Renaissance and even influenced modern science's formation. He is remembered as a polymath who contributed significantly to many knowledge areas. His work continues to be studied and admired for its breadth and depth.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
